From f46f8386ed887b04a33e5377ac31b8de168497ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: 2026-10-26T09:47:07Z
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: piano: drop the normal-mode RF clock vote


The WCN7860 power sequencer treats its optional clock as a dependency of
both WLAN and Bluetooth. Supplying RPMH_RF_CLK1 therefore requests the
RF buffer in active, wake and sleep states for as long as either radio
is powered, preventing the AP vote from being released during suspend.

On this board the stock WLAN node has no clock input. The stock Bluetooth
node describes this RF clock, but its driver only prepares and enables
it from perform_fmd_operation(), not from the normal radio power-on
path. It is not a normal-mode host-controlled clock dependency.

Remove the clock from the PMU node and let the connectivity subsystem
manage its normal clock demand. The sequencer already supports an absent
clock; GPIO and regulator sequencing is unchanged. Using the active-only
clock variant would still introduce a normal-mode AP vote absent from
the stock driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
@@ -326,8 +326,6 @@
 		vddrfa1p2-supply = <&vreg_s7i_1p31>;
 		vddrfa1p8-supply = <&vreg_s3g_1p86>;
 
-		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_RF_CLK1>;
-
 		status = "disabled";
 
 		regulators {

